From 620801e54117f36bd9e3c21f243b9ada7c68bf13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dico <248385067+AI-Dico@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:50:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Offer Hangul input on Korean Windows

The launcher passes tryomarchy.locale=ko_KR on Korean Windows, but the
guest only ships Chewing, so switching input methods gave Zhuyin and no
way to type Hangul. Ship fcitx5-hangul and, on Korean Windows, switch
fcitx5 profiles that are still the image default (as shipped, or as
fcitx5 5.1 saves it) to the US keyboard and Hangul before the display
manager starts. Edited, missing and linked profiles and other languages
are unchanged. Runtime 4.0.4-11 brings the package to existing disks with
the next Update > Omarchy, and revision 65 delivers the boot helper.
